### Repro steps

`++`/`--` on a member expression is lowered to a load, `+ 1`/`- 1` and a store, without converting the old value to a number first.

```jsx
function App() {
  return <Counter stored={{ count: "5" }} />;
}

function Counter({ stored }) {
  const state = { ...stored };
  state.count++;
  const t = { n: undefined };
  const old = t.n--;
  return <p>{state.count} {String(old)}</p>;
}
```

Render `<App />` with `renderToStaticMarkup`.

Expected (without the compiler): `<p>6 NaN</p>`
Actual (with the compiler): `<p>51 undefined</p>`

The output contains `state.count = state.count + 1;` and `t1 = t.n; t.n = t1 - 1;` with `old = t1`.

PRs #36991/#36992 fixed this by lowering member updates through a local `++`/`--`, but were closed by the stale bot without review. #35205 / #37347 is a different problem in the same lowering (postfix value).

### How often does this bug happen?

Every time

