## Bug description

In `next dev` the server embeds the “Instant Navigation Testing API” bootstrap into the
document. That inline script reads `document.cookie` **without a `try/catch`**:

```js
// dist/server/app-render/instant-test-bootstrap.js — getInstantTestBootstrapScriptContent()
if (document.cookie.indexOf("next-instant-navigation-testing=") > -1) {
  self.__next_instant_test = fetch(location.pathname + "?...", {});
}
```

It is appended to `bootstrapScriptContent` in `dist/server/app-render/app-render.js`
whenever `ctx.renderOpts.experimental.exposeTestingApi` is set, which is always the case in
dev (`dist/server/base-server.js`):

```js
exposeTestingApi: this.dev === true ||
  this.nextConfig.experimental.exposeTestingApiInProductionBuild === true;
```

Because the script runs before the client bootstrap, a throwing `document.cookie` getter
produces an uncaught exception and hydration never completes — the page ends on the global
error page (“This page couldn't load”). A form such as a login page becomes unusable.

A second unguarded access path exists on the client:

